---
layout: none
---
{%- comment -%}
  Index consumed by assets/js/arc42-search.js on /search/.

  No date field: 592c3b6 removed it deliberately. Jekyll fakes page.date from
  site.time for pages carrying none, which made every build differ.

  Only pages carrying a real title are indexed; that guard also drops the
  redirect stubs in _pages/ (which have no front-matter title) and the asset
  templates (sitemap, robots, the lunr JS), none of which are destinations.

  The separator is tracked in `sep` rather than via forloop.last: the loop skips
  entries, so forloop.last would be true for the wrong iteration whenever the
  final page is one of the skipped ones.

  Plain {% raw %}{% if %}{% endraw %} guards, not where_exp - github.com/arc42/arc42.org-site
  builds on GitHub Pages (Jekyll 3.10), not on the Jekyll 4.x pinned in the Gemfile.
{%- endcomment -%}
[
{%- assign sep = "" -%}
{%- for page in site.pages -%}
  {%- if page.title and page.title != "Sorry, Page Not Found (404)" -%}
{{ sep }}
  {
    "title"   : {{ page.title | jsonify }},
    "content" : {{ page.content | strip_html | strip_newlines | jsonify }},
    "url"     : {{ page.url | prepend: site.baseurl | jsonify }}
  }
    {%- assign sep = "," -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor %}
]
